  WebGL has no compute shaders, and Futhark only writes compute kernels. But the per-pixel work sits in two GPU functions taking only scalars, so each build gets a second entry point that calls them from a fragment shader.
  #note[A compile blocks WebGL; compiling first in a throwaway Worker fills the browser's shader cache, so the real compile then takes milliseconds.]
]

